Consolidate admin tooling under /admin behind a sidebar

The admin surface had two navigations and two homes. Seven working staff
pages lived under /account/admin/* behind AdminMenu, a wrapping strip of
black pills, while the surface added at admin.pana.social carried its own
hub of cards covering two mocked views. Neither knew the other existed.

Move the seven real pages to /admin/* and replace both navigations with one
sidebar in app/admin/layout.tsx.

Corrects a false claim. UNBUILT_TOOLS previously listed articles, contact
submissions, relay reports and mentoring as capability with no screen. All
four have had substantial screens the whole time, at /account/admin/*; the
list was written after searching app/api/admin/ and app/admin/ only. Of the
thirteen endpoints under app/api/admin/, the venue approve/suspend pair is
now the only one the sidebar cannot reach. The old menu's Events link had
neither a page nor an endpoint behind it and is dropped rather than carried.

Why a sidebar. The old strip needed two rows at 1280px and four at 430px,
and a row that grows sideways gets worse with every tool added. The sidebar
is 63px tall on mobile and groups the nine tools under Directory, Community,
Content and Inbox. Active state is an exact pathname match, not a prefix
match, because /admin prefixes every other route here.

The layout wraps real pages as well as mocked ones, so it carries no claim
about content. AdminMockBar stays inside the two mocked pages rather than
moving up, because "every number below is a fixture" sitting above the live
CSV export or the approval link that arrives in staff email would be wrong.

/account/admin/* paths keep working. Each is a redirect to its new home,
because staff notification emails already in inboxes point at the old URLs.
The two builders that generate those links now emit the new paths.

admin.pana.social/ redirects to /admin rather than rendering the overview
inline: app/page.tsx sits at the route tree root and so never receives
app/admin/layout.tsx, which would have served the one page without its nav.

The overview keeps no counts. Two tools are mocked and seven are real, and a
fixture figure sitting directly above links to live queues cannot be labelled
honestly in passing. It lists what each tool is for instead, as rows.

Not addressed, and worth a follow-up: these pages gate on `!session` rather
than on isAdmin, so any signed-in user renders the admin UI. The data behind
it is gated server-side, but the navigation is not. Left alone here because
moving the routes is already the change.

